From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grape <grape@invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:44:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tar: read only RAR and RAR5 in @archive mode

append_archive_filename() enabled every read format and every read
filter, then set mtree:checkfs after TAR_READER_OPTIONS had been
applied. Through @archive that let an input be read as mtree (which
opens local files named by contents= or by the entry's own path), as
a seekable ZIP that outbids RAR4 (issue #2249), or through a filter
that runs an external program found on PATH.

Enable only the rar and rar5 readers, enable no filter, and do not set
mtree:checkfs. TAR_READER_OPTIONS still applies (rar:hdrcharset=...).
Only append_archive_filename() changes; -x, -t and the disk reader are
untouched.

[Grape-owned patch. bsdtar is used only as
"bsdtar -c -P -f - --format pax @-".]
---
 tar/write.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tar/write.c b/tar/write.c
index 0f79dc9..37b7c31 100644
--- a/tar/write.c
+++ b/tar/write.c
@@ -644,10 +644,13 @@ append_archive_filename(struct bsdtar *bsdtar, struct archive *a,
 		filename = NULL; /* Library uses NULL for stdio. */
 
 	ina = archive_read_new();
-	archive_read_support_format_all(ina);
-	archive_read_support_filter_all(ina);
+	/* Grape: @archive reads RAR (v4 and v5) only. No other format
+	 * and no decompression filter, so no input can start an external
+	 * program, and no mtree, so no input can make bsdtar open a
+	 * local file. */
+	archive_read_support_format_rar(ina);
+	archive_read_support_format_rar5(ina);
 	set_reader_options(bsdtar, ina);
-	archive_read_set_options(ina, "mtree:checkfs");
 	if (bsdtar->passphrase != NULL)
 		rc = archive_read_add_passphrase(ina, bsdtar->passphrase);
 	else
